task (completed) {
  update news sources {source}

  Implemented:
  news_fetch.php
  - Added the `cbslite` source (https://www.cbc.ca/lite/news), parsed from
    the CBC Lite Next.js `__NEXT_DATA__` story list, with each linked CBC
    article page fetched and cached for the full detail view.
  - Added the `nprtext` source (https://text.npr.org/). The text-only
    homepage's `topic-title` links are parsed in listing order, and each
    lightweight NPR article page is fetched and cached for the full body,
    using the article's `paragraphs-container` prose (including the
    broadcast transcript) without the headline/byline/timestamp lines.
  - Both sources are full-article sources, so learned stories and the
    detail popup always receive real article text rather than a headline.
  app/chat_server.py
  - Added cbslite and nprtext to NEWS_SOURCES, so /news accepts them, the
    source picker and tab completion include them, and the /news help text
    lists them.

  Verified: `./news_fetch.php --json --source cbslite --limit 2` and
  `./news_fetch.php --json --source nprtext --limit 2` stream story cards
  with dates, summaries, and full paragraphs; `php -l news_fetch.php` and
  the Python syntax check both pass.
}

task.news_in_chat_global_corpus (completed) {
  please make sure the "learned" news are loaded as global corpus
  currently, we have messages like "11560 trunks from 535 videos", please do the same for news as well
  for every related trunk in the answer, have a "news" icon, when clicking on the icon, go to the related news, similar to the video trunks

  Implemented:
  chat.py
  - load_all_chunks() now merges .chat/news_cache trunks with the YouTube
  transcript corpus, so every learned story is searched by the same global
  BM25 index as the videos.
  - The startup line reports one combined summary, for example
  "Loaded 11,560 trunks from 534 video(s) and 1 news story(ies) for the
  global corpus."  /status uses the same video/news breakdown.
  - video_title() resolves a news story's saved headline, so BM25 prompts and
  answer annotations use the real story title.
  app/chat_server.py
  - /api/state includes a separate `news` count (and `videos` now counts only
  YouTube videos), and the server startup banner prints the combined
  corpus with both counts.
  - Answer annotations carry `kind: "news"` and the story's original URL
  for news chunks, so each related answer paragraph gets a news icon that
  opens the source story, matching the video icon behavior. Block-to-source
  scoring now uses IDF-weighted cosine similarity (a long transcript no
  longer wins just by sharing more common words), and a learned news source
  is preferred when it is nearly as close as the best transcript match.
  This keeps the news icon on a story even when a YouTube video paraphrases
  the same reporting.
  - refresh_news_corpus() makes a story learned from its /news modal part of
  the live global corpus immediately, and chunk_is_news() uses the news id
  pattern instead of a loose prefix check.
  app/chat.html
  - The status bar and welcome banner show the news story count next to the
  video count. Answer paragraphs sourced from a news trunk render the news
  icon (instead of the YouTube icon), with the story title as its tooltip.

  Verified: the learned CNN/Nvidia story contributes 31 trunks and is counted
  as 1 news story out of 535 sources overall; a query such as "what did Jensen
  Huang admit" ranks its news trunks first. Through the live server the answer
  event carried an annotation with `kind: "news"`, the story's CNN URL, and the
  story title, so the paragraph renders the news icon.
}

task.bug.news_chat_2_column_layout (completed) {
  please study the ui layout for youtube video popup modal, apply the same for news

  Implemented:
  app/chat.html
  - The story modal now uses the same two-column layout as the video modal:
  the article occupies a wide, independently scrolling left column, while
  the Learn/Chat action and the in-modal story conversation sit in a
  narrower right rail. The card widened from 760px to 1120px (up to 88vh)
  to match the video modal.
  - Below 760px the rail stacks under the article, and the whole layout
  scrolls as one pane instead of letting fixed-height grid rows overlap the
  article text.
  - Verified in headless Chromium at 1280x900 and 600x900: the article and
  rail render side by side on desktop with no page errors, the Learn/Chat
  controls and composer keep their natural height, and the article scrolls
  independently. The mobile layout stacks cleanly with no overlap.
}

task.bug.news_chat (completed) {
  bug:
  in the individual news popup modal:
  - when clicking on the "Chat" button:
  - expect: the chat message box show up
  - actual: the chat message box does not show up

  Root cause:
  The story modal is a flex column with a max-height. When a long article was
  rendered, the article body's huge flex base size consumed nearly all of the
  negative free space. `#news-chat` had the default `flex-shrink: 1` and
  `.video-chat` already sets `min-height: 0`, so the open chat collapsed to a
  ~15px sliver: its header showed, but the message list and compose box were
  clipped/overlapped by the article body.

  Implemented:
  app/chat.html
  - `#news-action` and `#news-chat` are now `flex: 0 0 auto`, so they keep
  their natural height when shown.
  - `.news-body` is now `flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 0`, so the long article
  absorbs all vertical shrinking and scrolls inside its own pane.

  Verified in headless Chromium with a 120-paragraph story: before the fix the
  open chat was 14.9px tall with its input rendered below the chat box; after
  the fix it is 199.6px tall, the input sits inside it, and the article body
  shrinks to 343.8px and scrolls.
}

task.news_chat (completed) {
  refactor, learn from youtube video chat:
  - please allow learning on a news, the news content and the learned news should be stored in {directory_of_this_prompt}/../.chat/news_cache
  - please allow chat on a specific news
  - in the chat, please include news in the global corpus as well

  Implemented:
  chat.py
  - Added .chat/news_cache to the corpus. Each learned story keeps a .json
  record, a readable .md copy, a .title file, an overview trunk (index 0),
  and one paragraph trunk per knowledge paragraph.
  - load_all_chunks() merges the transcript corpus with learned news trunks,
  and video_title() resolves news titles so BM25 indexing and prompts see
  the story headline.
  - Very small corpora can give every BM25 term a negative idf; top_chunks()
  now falls back to paragraph-level query-term overlap when no positive
  score exists, so a single learned story is still retrievable.
  app/chat_server.py
  - POST /api/news_learn stores the story content and builds its trunks in
  .chat/news_cache, then refreshes the global corpus immediately.
  - GET /api/news_status reports whether a story is already learned.
  - POST /api/news_chat answers from one learned story in an isolated session,
  using the same iterative RAG loop as transcript/video chat.
  - /news item events carry a stable news_id and learned flag; answers cite
  learned news with a news-source icon/link instead of a YouTube link.
  app/chat.html
  - The story modal now offers Learn, then Chat. Learned stories are marked
  in the feed list and can be re-opened and chatted with in place.
  - The in-modal story chat streams answers, supports dictionary lookups, and
  never disturbs the main chat's scope or conversation.
}

